Good, the .git/hooks directory exists with sample hooks. Now I'll create a pre-commit hook that runs mypy on all Python files in src/ and blocks the commit if type-checking fails.

The hook should:
1. Find all Python files in src/
2. Run mypy with the settings from pyproject.toml
3. Exit with a non-zero code if mypy fails to block the commit

Let me create the pre-commit hook script.
======================================================================

======================================================================
                              TOOL CALL                               
======================================================================
Function: execute_command
Arguments: {"command": "cat > .git/hooks/pre-commit << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\n# Pre-commit hook to run mypy type-checking on all Python files in src/\n\necho \"Running mypy type-checking on src/ directory...\"\n\n# Find all Python files in src/\nPYTHON_FILES=$(find src -name \"*.py\" -type f)\n\n# Run mypy with settings from pyproject.toml\nif ! mypy $PYTHON_FILES; then\n    echo \"\u274c mypy type-checking failed. Commit blocked.\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"\u2705 mypy type-checking passed.\"\nexit 0\nEOF"}
